        "description": "<div id=\"link_wrapped_content\">\n<body><section class=\"wp-block-bigbite-multi-title\"><div class=\"container\"></div></section>\n\n\n\n<p>Remember Sora? Developed by the powerhouse behind ChatGPT, Sora\u2019s AI-generated videos became instant social media sensations and spawned nightmares in Hollywood.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>But while the Sora demo reel blew away viewers back in February 2024 (a lifetime ago in the world of AI), OpenAI\u2019s gen-AI video platform failed to take off after a sluggish start. Now OpenAI says it will wind down its consumer Sora app.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>Sora confirmed the news in a <a href=\"https://x.com/soraofficialapp/status/2036532795984715896\">post on X</a>. \u201cWe\u2019re saying goodbye to Sora,\u201d says the post. \u201cWe\u2019ll share more soon, including timelines for the app and API and details on preserving your work.\u201d</p>\n\n\n\n<p>In a <a href=\"https://www.cbsnews.com/news/sora-ai-openai-discontinues/\">statement to CBS News</a>, OpenAI said the Sora team would continue its work on \u201cworld simulation research ",
